# netsurf: the APIs live on the interface prototypes; the engine's
# internals out of the page's sight (patch 276)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 275)
#
# In browsers navigator, screen, performance, crypto, history and
# screen.orientation have no own properties (Reflect.ownKeys(navigator) is
# [] in Chromium): their attributes are accessors and their operations
# methods of Navigator.prototype, Screen.prototype, ... The bridge made them
# plain objects with own members -- navigator 29, performance 17, history
# 13, screen 9 -- engine internals among them (__vitaHonest, __vitaNav,
# __vitaUserTiming, __setUrlDisplay, __traverse, ...), and
# Crypto.prototype.randomUUID did not exist (hsw checks for it and takes a
# different path without it).
#
#  - vita_polyfill.js, last section: each own member moves to the object's
#    interface prototype -- an operation as it is, a value as a read-only
#    accessor "get x" over this object's value (history.scrollRestoration
#    and on<event> handlers with a setter too); read through another
#    object it throws "Illegal invocation", as in Chromium.
#  - the polyfill's own state about objects -- the marks it puts on its
#    wrappers (__vbCD, __vbNat, __vbHat, ...) and per-element state
#    (selection, custom validity, <details>/<dialog> expandos, canvas
#    contexts) -- moves from properties of those functions and elements to
#    a private per-object record (PV(), a WeakMap on __vitaPriv), so
#    Object.getOwnPropertyNames(element.matches) is length, name. Patch
#    275's stand-ins share their original's record. Left as they are:
#    __vbNS (set by the bridge in C) and the window globals the bridge
#    calls by name (__vbTapFocus, __vbSelectorMatch, __vbCustomEl).
#  - navigator / performance flags -> __vitaPriv (not enumerable).
#  - macsurf_qjs.c: history's engine hooks (__setUrlDisplay,
#    __nativeLength, __traverse, __atForwardEnd, __hasPushState) live on
#    __vitaHistory (not enumerable) and every caller (the L/R traversal,
#    the pushState shim) uses it; the EventTarget shim keeps listeners in
#    a WeakMap instead of an own __msEventTargetListeners.
#
# Not in this patch: document (136 own members, internals among them) and
# elements (tagName / nodeName / nodeType / __ptr own) -- several document
# objects exist at once (DOMParser, createHTMLDocument), which needs its
# own care.
#
# Found by the hCaptcha record/compare (docs/wasm-hcaptcha-measurement.md,
# "Record, replay"); Chromium given this engine's own-property layout still
# passes, and the demo still refuses the engine.
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-api-protos.html (APIPROTO 7/7, Chromium 7/7;
# the build before fails at least 1, 2, 3, 7).
